---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Website Design for Coaches | Brighter Sites"
  description="Custom website design for life coaches, career coaches, ADHD and executive-function coaches, relationship coaches, and other independent coaching practices."
>
  <section class="page-intro">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">Website design for coaches</p>

      <h1>Your coaching website should make it clear who you help and why working with you is different.</h1>

      <p class="page-lead">
        Brighter Sites builds custom websites for coaches whose work depends on
        trust, expertise, and a strong personal connection. Whether you offer
        life coaching, career coaching, executive-function support, relationship
        coaching, or another specialized service, your website should help the
        right person quickly understand what you do and whether you may be a good
        fit.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section tint">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">Make the offer understandable</p>

        <h2>Coaching can be difficult to explain in one sentence. Your website has more room.</h2>

        <p>
          Prospective clients often need to understand the problem you help
          solve, what working with you actually looks like, and what makes your
          approach different from other coaches they have found online. A clear
          website gives that information a useful structure instead of asking
          visitors to piece it together themselves.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="feature-grid">
        <article class="feature">
          <h3>Define who you help</h3>
          <p>
            Clear positioning helps visitors understand whether your coaching is
            designed for their goals, challenges, stage of life, or particular
            situation.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="feature">
          <h3>Explain how you work</h3>
          <p>
            One-on-one sessions, programs, packages, consultations, workshops,
            virtual services, and other offers should be easy to understand
            before someone contacts you.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="feature">
          <h3>Build confidence before the call</h3>
          <p>
            Your background, approach, process, frequently asked questions, and
            next steps can answer important questions before a prospective
            client schedules a conversation.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container service-detail-grid">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Different coaching practices need different sites</p>
        <h2>The structure should follow your business—not a generic coaching template.</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="detail-list">
        <div>
          <h3>Life and personal-development coaching</h3>
          <p>
            Your website can connect your approach to the changes clients are
            trying to make while giving them a realistic picture of what working
            together involves.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h3>ADHD and executive-function coaching</h3>
          <p>
            Visitors may be looking for help with organization, planning,
            routines, accountability, or follow-through. Clear service pages can
            make those areas of support easier to find and understand.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h3>Career and professional coaching</h3>
          <p>
            Career transitions, leadership development, job-search support, and
            professional growth can each require different messaging and calls
            to action.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h3>Relationship, parenting, grief, and recovery coaching</h3>
          <p>
            More personal areas of coaching require thoughtful language,
            appropriate boundaries, and a website that communicates support
            without overstating what the service provides.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section tint">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">Built to support growth</p>

        <h2>Your website should keep working after the first version goes live.</h2>

        <p>
          Brighter Sites builds the technical foundation for search visibility,
          mobile usability, measurement, and future improvements so your website
          can evolve as your coaching business develops.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="feature-grid">
        <article class="feature">
          <h3>Search-focused structure</h3>
          <p>
            Focused pages can give important coaching specialties and services a
            clear place in the site instead of relying on one broad homepage to
            explain everything.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="feature">
          <h3>Clear conversion paths</h3>
          <p>
            Consultation requests, discovery calls, contact forms, program
            inquiries, and other next steps can be placed where they make sense
            in the visitor's decision process.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="feature">
          <h3>Useful measurement</h3>
          <p>
            Search and website data can help identify what people are finding,
            which pages receive attention, and where changes may improve the
            experience.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>

      <p style="margin-top:2rem">
        <a class="text-link" href="/website-strategy/">
          Learn about SEO, analytics, and website strategy →
        </a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="cta-panel">
        <p class="eyebrow">Build around your coaching practice</p>

        <h2>Give prospective clients a clear reason to keep reading.</h2>

        <p>
          Tell me what kind of coaching you provide, who you work with, and how
          clients currently find you. We can build the website around the
          questions those prospective clients actually need answered.
        </p>

        <a class="button" href="/contact/">Talk about your coaching website</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
